DESCRIPTION:Sign up!\nThe Lovestruck Balladeers enchant audiences with their masterful performances and inspired repertoire of ragtime\, jazz and beautiful songs from around the world. Born out of New York’s vibrant classic jazz and traditional music scene\, The Lovestruck Balladeers formed during a series of recording sessions for Jalopy Records' 2018 release\, Estrellas de Radio.  Since their debut at The Brooklyn Folk Festival that same year\,  the versatile quintet has made a name for itself as a compelling act highlighting musical excellence\, fresh arrangements\, original songs and a tightly crafted stage show.\nThe Lovestruck Balladeers are Jake Sanders\, Dennis Lichtman\, Sean Cronin and Dalton Ridenhour.  Featuring special guest Mike Davis.\n\nLink: https://www.barnevents.info/events/2026/1/14/dance-party-with-the-lovestruck-balladeers
DTEND:20260418T020000Z
LOCATION:The Barn
DTSTART:20260418T000000Z
SUMMARY:🎵 [Jazz] Dance Party with The Lovestruck Balladeers
UID:288129c2-b822-41c5-a9c2-3187be285c81@2881.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Sign Up\nSugar Britches is a blend of mischievous high-brow honky-tonk with eclectic instrumental accompaniment and clever lyrics\, written by Brian Johanson and performed by a cavalcade of characters. Combining good ‘ol country heartache along with snarky folksy wit\, Sugar Britches has been playing non-stop throughout Colorado and the great West in bars\, parking lots\, weddings\, bat mitzvahs\, rodeos\, amphitheaters and regular-ass theaters since 2017.Sugar Britches have received critical acclaim and plain old criticism\, from music lovers and mothers. They have won hearts and minds and driven audiences wild with their sex appeal\, fanciful stylings and wit. They have opened up for many national touring artists\, including Reckless Kelly\, Wynonna Judd & the Big Noise\, Hannah Dasher\, Jaime Wyatt\, Big Richard\, Midland\, Billy Bob Thornton and the Boxmasters\, Pokey LaFarge\, Corb Lund\, The Reverend Horton Heat and Jason Eady.The band released their first album\, Don’t Make Her a Mixtape Yet You Idiot\, in 2019\, their second album\, No One Cares That It’s Your Birthday in 2022\, and they are currently recording their 3rd AND 4th albums as you read this (check out our Indiegogo campaign). The Band features Brian Johanson on lead vocals and guitar\, Lance Ruby on lead electric guitar\, AJ Knight on drums\, Cameron Collums on upright bass and a rotating cast of amazing guest musicians. Keep your eyes peeled for all of our special guests and show iterations.\nYes\, there will be dancing!\n\nLink: https://www.barnevents.info/events/2025/6/27/sugar-britches
DTEND:20260530T020000Z
LOCATION:The Barn
DTSTART:20260530T000000Z
SUMMARY:🎵 [Rock] Sugar Britches
UID:f67dcc2b-f382-4181-b030-d7348f94ab21@f67d.org
END:VEVENT
